## CHART CONSTRUCTION (CANONICAL)

This is the core of the skill. Native Chart.js does not draw % inside donut
slices nor a value next to bars — the two plugins below solve that and
are **100% generic** (zero brand dependency). Registered globally,
**inert until a chart opts in** (`options.plugins.<id> = { display:true }`).
Copy them verbatim — do not reimplement.

```javascript
// slicePercent — draws "XX.X%" INSIDE each donut/pie slice.
const slicePercent = {
  id: 'slicePercent',
  afterDatasetsDraw(chart, args, opts) {
    if (!opts.display) return
    const { ctx } = chart
    const meta = chart.getDatasetMeta(0)
    const data = chart.data.datasets[0].data
    const total = data.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)
    const minPct = opts.minPct ?? 3
    meta.data.forEach((arc, i) => {
      const pct = (data[i] / total) * 100
      if (pct < minPct) return
      const pos = arc.tooltipPosition()
      ctx.save()
      ctx.font = '700 11px ' + (opts.fontFamily || 'sans-serif')
      ctx.fillStyle = '#fff'
      ctx.textAlign = 'center'
      ctx.textBaseline = 'middle'
      ctx.shadowColor = 'rgba(0,0,0,.6)'
      ctx.shadowBlur = 2
      ctx.fillText(pct.toFixed(1).replace('.', ',') + '%', pos.x, pos.y)
      ctx.restore()
    })
  },
}

// barValue — draws the raw value ABOVE vertical bars (bar.x, bar.y-4,
// center/bottom) or NEXT TO horizontal bars (bar.x+6, bar.y,
// left/middle). Auto-detects indexAxis==='y'; ignores 'line' datasets in
// mixed charts. Horizontal bars REQUIRE layout.padding.right:90
// so the label is not clipped.
const barValue = {
  id: 'barValue',
  afterDatasetsDraw(chart, args, opts) {
    if (!opts.display) return
    const { ctx } = chart
    const isHorizontal = chart.options.indexAxis === 'y'
    chart.data.datasets.forEach((ds, dsIndex) => {
      if (ds.type === 'line') return
      const meta = chart.getDatasetMeta(dsIndex)
      meta.data.forEach((bar, i) => {
        const value = ds.data[i]
        const label = (opts.format || String)(value, ds, i)
        ctx.save()
        ctx.font = '600 10.5px ' + (opts.fontFamily || 'sans-serif')
        ctx.fillStyle = opts.color || '#E5E7EB'
        ctx.shadowColor = 'rgba(0,0,0,.6)'
        ctx.shadowBlur = 2
        if (isHorizontal) {
          ctx.textAlign = 'left'
          ctx.textBaseline = 'middle'
          ctx.fillText(label, bar.x + 6, bar.y)
        } else {
          ctx.textAlign = 'center'
          ctx.textBaseline = 'bottom'
          ctx.fillText(label, bar.x, bar.y - 4)
        }
        ctx.restore()
      })
    })
  },
}

Chart.register(slicePercent, barValue)
```

**Hard invariants (per chart type):**

- Every donut/pie: `responsive:true, maintainAspectRatio:false`, slices
  `borderColor: 'var(--bg-body)' , borderWidth:2`, `slicePercent:{display:true}`,
  localized tooltip, `cutout:'55-65%'`.
- Every bar: `borderRadius:6`; horizontal adds `indexAxis:'y'` +
  `layout.padding.right:90` + `barValue`.
- Line: `tension:0.3`, `animation:false`, `applyChartWipe(el,1300)` right after
  `new Chart` (the animation belongs to the CSS wipe — see ANIMATIONS section).
- Radar: fill = `var(--accent)` with alpha, solid border `var(--accent)`,
  `pointRadius:4`, `r` axis `max:100`.
- **Lifecycle:** dict-of-charts + `destroy()` at the top of each render +
  recreate. **Never `chart.update()`.**

