## ANIMATIONS

The system rests on **3 mechanisms only**:

1. **Native default Chart.js animation** for `bar` / `doughnut` / `radar` /
   `combo` — never declare an `animation` block, never touch
   `Chart.defaults.animation` (default = 1000ms `easeOutQuart`).
2. **CSS wipe via `clip-path`** for `line` charts — they carry
   `animation:false` and call `applyChartWipe(canvasEl, 1300)` right after
   `new Chart`.
3. **Lazy-render per tab** (`tabRenderers` + `tabStale`) so the entry
   animation fires only when the canvas is visible. Never instantiate a
   chart inside a hidden `.tab-content{display:none}`.

### Canonical tokens

- **Easing:** `cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)` (used by the line wipe).
- **Wipe duration:** `1300ms`. **Pulse (status dot):** `2s infinite`.
  **Hover/UI transitions:** `all .2s`.
- **No stagger, no per-element delay, no count-up, no IntersectionObserver,
  no requestAnimationFrame.**

### The ONLY two CSS @keyframes

```css
@keyframes pulse{50%{opacity:.4}}
@keyframes chartWipeLR{from{clip-path:inset(0 100% 0 0);-webkit-clip-path:inset(0 100% 0 0)}to{clip-path:inset(0 0 0 0);-webkit-clip-path:inset(0 0 0 0)}}
.chart-wipe-anim{animation-name:chartWipeLR;animation-timing-function:cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);animation-fill-mode:forwards;will-change:clip-path}
.dot{animation:pulse 2s infinite}
```

### Line wipe helper (core)

```javascript
function applyChartWipe(canvas, duration) {
  if (!canvas) return
  canvas.classList.remove('chart-wipe-anim')
  void canvas.offsetWidth // force reflow so the keyframe re-triggers on re-render
  canvas.style.animationDuration = (duration || 1300) + 'ms'
  canvas.classList.add('chart-wipe-anim')
}
```

### Hover & Entry — NO DISPLACEMENT (canonical law)

Motion belongs to the **chart** (wipe/grow/rotate), never to the **layout**. Cards
do not travel; sections do not slide.

**(a) Hover NEVER displaces.** No card `:hover` uses
`transform`/`translate`/`translateY`/`scale`. The feedback is a **fade of
`background-color`**, optionally `border-color`:

```css
.kpi-card, .chart-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
    transition: background-color .2s, border-color .2s;  /* DO NOT use transition:all */
}
.kpi-card:hover, .chart-card:hover {
    background-color: var(--hover);
    border-color: var(--accent);   /* optional */
    /* NO transform, NO translateY, NO lift */
}
```

**(b) Page/tab/section entry NEVER displaces.** No `translateY`, no
`fadeInUp`, no slide. Entry = **opacity fade only**
(`opacity:0→1`, no transform) **or nothing**. Tab switching stays hard
`display:none`↔`block`; the perceived transition is the entry animation of
the opened tab's chart.

**(c) CHART animations remain.** bar grows from the baseline, doughnut
sweeps the arc (rotate), radar scales from the center, `line` uses the wipe
`chartWipeLR` (clip-path), combo draws together. These move the **drawn
data**, not the container — that is why they are permitted and approved.

> KPI numbers are written with `textContent` directly — they are **not**
> animated (no count-up).

